# Supabase SQL

## Migrations

- Files: `supabase/migrations/NNNN_description.sql` — sequential, never edit applied migrations.
- Header comment block per file; one concern per migration.
- Apply via `supabase db push` or SQL editor in order.

## Security model

- **RLS enabled** on every table. Policies use `is_org_member`, `has_org_role`, `can_access_venture`.
- **SECURITY DEFINER** helpers live in `0001_foundation.sql`; reuse them — avoid recursive policy subqueries.
- New tables with venture data: add `venture_id` FK + policy via `can_access_venture`.
- New org-scoped tables: add `org_id` FK + `is_org_member(org_id)` policies.

## RPCs (existing)

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `add_member_by_email` | Invite existing user to org (owner/admin only) |
| `create_workspace` | New org + owner membership for caller |
| `bootstrap_my_workspace` | Self-heal missing workspace on first load |

New privileged operations → RPC with `security definer` + role checks, not client-side inserts.

## Grants

```sql
grant execute on function public.my_function(...) to authenticated;
```

## After schema changes

Update `src/lib/types.ts` if new columns/tables affect the app. No generated Supabase types in this repo yet.
